--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
0. SCOPE / PARITY READING (web source read end-to-end)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
AIThinkingIndicator.tsx is a PURE presentational streaming-empty indicator. Its only
data input is `useTranslation`; it fetches nothing. Its real render branches are:
  • leading label = `label ?? t('helix.thinking','Helix is thinking')`  (override vs default)
  • the AI-common verb default the prop doc references: `t('ai.common.thinking','AI is thinking')`
  • Reduce-Motion variant (web `motion-safe:`): glyph stops pulsing, dots stop bouncing,
    lines drop the shimmer — the static skeleton stays visible.
  • a pulsing brand HelixMark, three staggered bouncing dots, three decreasing-width
    (w-full / w-11/12 / w-9/12) shimmer lines.
  • a11y: role="status" + aria-live="polite"; dots + lines are aria-hidden.
  • a compact in-button sibling `AIThinkingDots({ label })` (bg-current dots).
There is NO query/empty/error/stale/offline DATA envelope in the source, so those generic
template states are N/A for this surface (same disposition as the sanctioned ToolCard
precedent — "ToolCard is a pure presentational container; the web source fetches nothing").
Every REAL branch above is reproduced. No scope narrowing.

Native HelixMark counterpart = SF Symbol `sparkles` + cyan accent tint, matching the
sibling AISettings `HelixIconBox`. The brand-mark ATOM is owned by the P4 component-library
bundle (out of scope here), so it is rendered inline within the allowed surface files.

